{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"quarantine=aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '-- candidate tail --'\nsed -n '300,620p' \\\"\"'$quarantine/AristotleCandidates/ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '-- remote summary --'\nsed -n '1,260p' \\\"\"'$quarantine/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '-- archive differences excluding intended module/response --'\ndiff -qr --exclude='.lake' --exclude='lake-manifest.json' --exclude='ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean' . \\\"\"'$quarantine\" | sed -n '\"'1,260p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '-- forbidden candidate tokens --'\nrg -n '\\\\b(sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|implemented_by|native_decide)\\\\b' \\\"\"'$quarantine/AristotleCandidates/ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean\" || true\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '-- imports resolution --'\nfor p in AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean AristotleCandidates/ConcreteCStarCompletion.lean; do test -f \\\"\"'$p\" && echo \"present $p\" || echo \"MISSING $p\"; done'","aggregated_output":"-- candidate tail --\n\n/-- **Faithfulness.**  An isometric family of stage representations induces an\ninjective (faithful) embedding of the algebraic quasilocal limit into the\nconcrete C⋆-algebra. -/\ntheorem injective_embedding : Function.Injective R.embedding :=\n  injective_quasilocalEmbedding R.rho R.compat R.injective_rho\n\n/-- **Dense embedding.** -/\ntheorem denseRange_embedding : DenseRange R.embedding :=\n  denseRange_quasilocalEmbedding R.rho R.compat\n\n/-- The concrete C⋆-algebra is the closure of the union of the finite-stage\noperator ranges. -/\ntheorem coe_cstarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion :\n    ((R.cstarAlgebra : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) =\n      closure (⋃ i, Set.range (R.rho i)) :=\n  coe_quasilocalCStarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion R.rho R.compat\n\n/-- Minimality of the concrete C⋆-algebra. -/\ntheorem cstarAlgebra_isLeast :\n    IsLeast {S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H) |\n        IsClosed (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∧ ∀ i x, R.rho i x ∈ S} R.cstarAlgebra :=\n  quasilocalCStarAlgebra_isLeast R.rho R.compat\n\nomit [IsDirectedOrder ι] [Nonempty ι] [DirectedSystem A fun x1 x2 x3 => ⇑(f x1 x2 x3)] in\ninclude R in\n/-- The connecting maps of the directed system are isometric, hence in\nparticular injective, as soon as the stage representations are. -/\ntheorem norm_map_connecting (i j : ι) (h : i ≤ j) (x : A i) : ‖f i j h x‖ = ‖x‖ := by\n  rw [← R.norm_rho j, R.compat i j h x, R.norm_rho i]\n\nend IsometricStageRepresentation\n\nend Isometric\n\n/-! ## Non-vacuity of the hypotheses -/\n\nsection NonVacuity\n\nvariable (H : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- The constant directed system all of whose stages are the bounded operators on `H`. -/\nabbrev constStage : ℕ → Type _ := fun _ => H →L[ℂ] H\n\n/-- The identity connecting maps of the constant directed system. -/\nnoncomputable def constConnecting :\n    ∀ i j : ℕ, i ≤ j → constStage H i →⋆ₐ[ℂ] constStage H j :=\n  fun _ _ _ => StarAlgHom.id ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)\n\nnoncomputable instance : DirectedSystem (constStage H) (constConnecting H · · ·) :=\n  ⟨fun _ _ => rfl, fun _ _ _ _ _ _ => rfl⟩\n\n/-- The hypotheses of `IsometricStageRepresentation` are satisfiable: the identity\nrepresentation of the constant system of bounded operators on `H` is an explicitly\nfaithful isometric stage representation. -/\nnoncomputable def idIsometricStageRepresentation :\n    IsometricStageRepresentation (constStage H) (constConnecting H) H where\n  rho _ := StarAlgHom.id ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)\n  compat _ _ _ _ := rfl\n  norm_rho _ _ := rfl\n\nend NonVacuity\n\n/-! ## The dyadic specialization -/\n\nsection Dyadic\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\nvariable (D : QubitOperatorRepresentationData H)\n\n/-- The concrete quasilocal C⋆-algebra attached to a compatible family of\nfinite-qubit-stage representations: the closed operator range of the induced\nrepresentation of the algebraic UHF limit `QubitUHFAlgebra`.\n\nBoth the Hilbert space and the stage representations are supplied input; no\ninfinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed. -/\nnoncomputable def qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H) :=\n  quasilocalCStarAlgebra D.rho D.compat\n\n/-- The canonical embedding of the algebraic UHF limit into its concrete\nquasilocal C⋆-algebra. -/\nnoncomputable def qubitQuasilocalEmbedding :\n    QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra D :=\n  quasilocalEmbedding D.rho D.compat\n\n/-- Finite-stage formula for the dyadic concrete embedding. -/\n@[simp] theorem coe_qubitQuasilocalEmbedding_of (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n) :\n    (qubitQuasilocalEmbedding D\n        (DirectLimit.Module.of ℂ ℕ QubitTensorPower qubitTensorPowerMap n x) :\n      H →L[ℂ] H) = D.rho n x :=\n  coe_quasilocalEmbedding_of D.rho D.compat n x\n\n/-- Finite-stage formula for the dyadic concrete embedding, applied to a\nvector. -/\ntheorem qubitQuasilocalEmbedding_of_apply (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n) (v : H) :\n    (qubitQuasilocalEmbedding D\n        (DirectLimit.Module.of ℂ ℕ QubitTensorPower qubitTensorPowerMap n x) :\n      H →L[ℂ] H) v = D.rho n x v :=\n  quasilocalEmbedding_of_apply D.rho D.compat n x v\n\n/-- **Dense embedding** of the algebraic UHF limit in the dyadic concrete\nquasilocal C⋆-algebra. -/\ntheorem denseRange_qubitQuasilocalEmbedding :\n    DenseRange (qubitQuasilocalEmbedding D) :=\n  denseRange_quasilocalEmbedding D.rho D.compat\n\n/-- **Conditional faithfulness** for the dyadic model: if every supplied\nfinite-qubit-stage representation is injective, the concrete embedding is\ninjective. -/\ntheorem injective_qubitQuasilocalEmbedding (h_inj : ∀ n, Function.Injective (D.rho n)) :\n    Function.Injective (qubitQuasilocalEmbedding D) :=\n  injective_quasilocalEmbedding D.rho D.compat h_inj\n\n/-- The dyadic concrete algebra is the closure of the union of the\nfinite-qubit-stage operator ranges. -/\ntheorem coe_qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion :\n    ((qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra D : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n      Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = closure (⋃ n : ℕ, Set.range (D.rho n)) :=\n  coe_quasilocalCStarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion D.rho D.compat\n\n/-- Minimality of the dyadic concrete algebra. -/\ntheorem qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra_isLeast :\n    IsLeast {S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H) |\n        IsClosed (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∧ ∀ n x, D.rho n x ∈ S}\n      (qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra D) :=\n  quasilocalCStarAlgebra_isLeast D.rho D.compat\n\nend Dyadic\n\nend ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel\nend StabilizerHyperfinite\n-- remote summary --\n# Summary of changes for run 15cd2dcc-57a9-41d6-b198-a01b1bf3a872\nCreated the single new module `AristotleCandidates/ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean`. `lake build AristotleCandidates.ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel` succeeds with no warnings, the file contains no `sorry`/`admit`/`axiom`/`opaque`/`unsafe`/`implemented_by`, and the main theorems depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\n**What was built (checked infrastructure, combining P37's algebraic-limit operator representation with the previously checked closed operator-range construction).**\n\nConcrete model: `quasilocalCStarAlgebra rho compat := (algebraicLimitOperatorRep rho compat).range.topologicalClosure`, a closed star-subalgebra of `H →L[ℂ] H` carrying a genuine `CStarAlgebra` instance, together with the canonical star-algebra homomorphism `quasilocalEmbedding : DirectLimit A f →⋆ₐ[ℂ] quasilocalCStarAlgebra`.\n\nProved about it:\n- finite-stage formulas `coe_quasilocalEmbedding_of` (`embedding (of i x) = rho i x` as an operator) and `quasilocalEmbedding_of_apply` (evaluated on a vector);\n- `denseRange_quasilocalEmbedding` (dense embedding) and `denseRange_stage_images`;\n- `range_algebraicLimitOperatorRep` and `coe_quasilocalCStarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion`: the concrete algebra is exactly the closure of the union of the finite-stage operator ranges (the quasilocality statement);\n- `injective_quasilocalEmbedding` (faithfulness), `quasilocalCStarAlgebra_le` / `quasilocalCStarAlgebra_isLeast` (minimality among closed star-subalgebras containing all stage ranges), and `norm_star_mul_self_limitRep` (C*-identity for limit elements).\n\nIsometric input package: the structure `IsometricStageRepresentation` with the derived results `isometry_rho`, `injective_rho`, `norm_embedding_of` (finite-stage norm formula `‖embedding (of i x)‖ = ‖x‖`), `injective_embedding` (unconditional faithfulness given the structure's fields), `denseRange_embedding`, `coe_cstarAlgebra_eq_closure_iUnion`, `cstarAlgebra_isLeast`, and `norm_map_connecting` (the connecting maps are isometric). Non-vacuity is witnessed by `idIsometricStageRepresentation` (identity representation of the constant system of bounded operators).\n\nDyadic specialization: for the supplied `QubitOperatorRepresentationData H`, `qubitQuasilocalCStarAlgebra` / `qubitQuasilocalEmbedding` of the algebraic UHF limit `QubitUHFAlgebra`, with the finite-qubit-stage formulas, dense range, closure-of-union description, minimality, and faithfulness conditional on injectivity of each `D.rho n`.\n\n**Exact faithfulness/isometry assumptions used.**\n1. General section: an explicitly supplied complex Hilbert space `H` (`NormedAddCommGroup`, `InnerProductSpace ℂ`, `CompleteSpace`), supplied stage representations `rho i : A i →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)`, and compatibility `compat : ∀ i j (h : i ≤ j) x, rho j (f i j h x) = rho i x`. Faithfulness of the embedding is stated conditionally on the explicit premise `h_inj : ∀ i, Function.Injective (rho i)`.\n2. Isometric section: the same data for normed stage algebras (`NormedRing (A i)`, `StarRing (A i)`, `NormedAlgebra ℂ (A i)`), plus the structure field `norm_rho : ∀ i a, ‖rho i a‖ = ‖a‖`. This single isometry field yields stage injectivity and hence faithfulness of the limit embedding, and the finite-stage norm formula.\n3. Dyadic section: the P37 data fields `rho n : QubitTensorPower n →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H)` and `compat` with `qubitTensorPowerMap`; since the qubit stages carry no norm instances in the project, faithfulness there is stated with the explicit premise `∀ n, Function.Injective (D.rho n)` (no isometry statement is claimed for that case).\n\n**Boundary respected.** The representation remains supplied input; nothing claims an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space, a regional C*-isomorphism, GNS factorization, normality, bicommutant, or factor classification. No source or Mathlib obstruction was encountered for this packet.-- archive differences excluding intended module/response --\nOnly in .: .git\nOnly in aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle: ARISTOTLE_SOURCE_CONTEXT.md\nOnly in aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle: ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\nOnly in aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle: AUTONOMY_POLICY.md\nFiles ./README.md and aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle/README.md differ\nOnly in .: aristotle_responses\nOnly in aristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle: manuscript\n-- forbidden candidate tokens --\n-- imports resolution --\npresent AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean\npresent AristotleCandidates/ConcreteCStarCompletion.lean\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
